<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>dev.wingmen.cubeasht-daily-digest</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key><array><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/.venv/bin/python3</string><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/scripts/cubeasht_daily_digest.py</string></array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key><dict><key>HOME</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa</string><key>PATH</key><string>/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string></dict>
  <!-- cc-fleet-health cubeasht DAILY HEALTH DIGEST (operator ask#2207, Nazim bus
       #64620/#64628). Once a day it summarizes the PRIOR complete UTC day of
       cubeasht host_metrics (temps / CPU load busy-vs-idle / RAM) and posts a
       calm roll-up to the bus (orch-console). The 5-min dev.wingmen.cubeasht-monitor
       job PAGES on breaches; this is the quiet backstop so slow drift surfaces.
       The script load_dotenv's $ORCH/.env for DATABASE_URL and posts via
       scripts/bus_send.send() (cc-fleet-health has no TG pen) -- no secrets here.
       Dedup is one-digest-per-summarized-date in logs/cubeasht_daily_digest_state.json.

       TIME: targets 09:00 Asia/Dubai (the operator's morning, same slot as
       asks-daily-digest). StartCalendarInterval's Hour fires in the HOST's
       local zone, which is Asia/Singapore (UTC+8) on this Mac Mini -- NOT UTC
       and NOT UAE (bus #44286: asks-daily-digest once fired 8h off by assuming
       a UTC host clock). 09:00 Asia/Dubai = 05:00 UTC = 13:00 SGT -> Hour=13
       below (Minute=5 staggers it off asks-daily-digest's :00). At 05:00 UTC
       the prior UTC day is fully complete, so the default "yesterday UTC"
       summary always has a whole day of samples. tests/
       test_launchd_uae_calendar_hours.py recomputes this from zoneinfo and
       fails loud if the Hour drifts. If this host's clock ever moves zones,
       recompute Hour there and here.

       NOT launchctl-loaded by landing this file -- a separate go-live step
       `launchctl load`s it (and can `kickstart` the first fire). -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key><dict><key>Hour</key><integer>13</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>5</integer></dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/logs/cubeasht-daily-digest.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/logs/cubeasht-daily-digest.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
